language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find a fifth number (at least 0) such that the product of it with any of the numbers 1, 3, 8, 120 is one less than a perfect square.
given n : int(1..)
given max_val : int(0..)
$ the three given numbers of the set and 1 (the first four members of the set)
letting Members = [1, 3, 8, 120]
$ the fifth number, searched in 0 to max_val
find number : int(0..max_val)
$ roots[i] is the square root of (Members[i] times number plus one)
find roots : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..11*max_val)

such that
$ the product of the fifth number with 1, 3, 8 and 120 is one less than a perfect square
forAll i : int(1..4) . (roots[i] * roots[i] = Members[i] * number + 1)
